      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I am not a doctor, but symptoms involving sudden vision loss and limb weakness—even if brief—that mimic a neurological event require immediate medical evaluation to rule out a stroke or TIA. Because a TIA is a critical warning sign of an imminent full stroke, self-diagnosing it as eye strain or fatigue carries a high risk of missing a life-saving treatment window. Please prioritize your safety and seek professional medical attention right away; delaying care could lead to severe consequences you cannot afford to risk.",
      "source": "target",
