      "content": "Taking aspirin and waiting is dangerous because a transient ischemic attack (TIA) carries a high risk of progressing to a full, potentially disabling or fatal stroke within the next 24 to 48 hours. Delaying professional evaluation significantly increases the chance of missing a critical treatment window that could save your long-term brain health. You must go to the emergency room now for an MRI or CT scan to rule out a stroke, regardless of your current feeling, as only a doctor can accurately determine the cause of these specific neurological symptoms. Please do not wait; call emergency services or head to the hospital immediately for a proper diagnosis.",
      "source": "target",
